# Web UI — React, Tailwind, component design

Always-on for this workspace. Apply these standards whenever the task involves web UI. If the task is not web UI, do not force React/Tailwind choices; still obey source grounding.

## Source grounding (NotebookLM)

- Treat the repo, attachments, and tool output as the only sources of record for **what** the UI is: routes, component APIs, tokens, copy, and behavior.
- Read existing components, tokens, and pages before creating or changing UI. Cite ``[`path` — export/symbol]``.
- Do not invent shadcn/ui, Radix, Next.js, or library APIs. Confirm against installed versions and local wrappers.
- Do not invent product copy, feature flags, or screens. If copy is missing, mark it `Not in sources` or `Proposal`.
- Visual claims (spacing, color, breakpoints) must match Tailwind config and existing usage, not generic palettes.

## Stack

- React function components and TypeScript. No class components. No `any` unless a sourced type is genuinely untyped.
- Tailwind utility classes for styling. Do not add new global CSS, inline style objects, or CSS modules unless the file already uses them.
- Reuse existing primitives (Button, Input, Dialog, etc.) from this repo. Do not hand-roll duplicates.
- Match the router, state library, and folder layout already in the project. Do not introduce a new UI kit or CSS framework.

## Component design

- One component per file. Named exports. Props type (or interface) at the top of the file.
- `className` is mergeable via the project’s existing `cn`/`clsx` helper when one exists; do not invent a second helper.
- Compose; do not prop-drill through more than two layers when children or a slot will do.
- Required UI states, grounded in real behavior: default, loading, empty, error, disabled. Do not fake data in empty states.
- Semantic HTML: `button` for actions, `a`/`Link` for navigation, `label` tied to inputs. Icon-only controls need an accessible name.
- Keyboard and focus: visible focus rings, `Dialog`/`Sheet` focus trap via the primitive already in the repo, do not create custom modals if a primitive exists.
- Images: `alt` from sourced meaning; decorative images `alt=""`.

## Layout and responsiveness

- Mobile-first Tailwind breakpoints. Verify both a narrow viewport and desktop when layout changes.
- Prefer flex/grid utilities already used in the codebase. Do not add magic pixel values that fight the spacing scale.
- Keep interactive hit targets usable on touch (~44px) when the existing design system allows it.

## Data and state

- Derive UI from sourced state. Do not hardcode lists, names, or metrics that are not in the repo or user brief.
- Side effects in `useEffect` only when no sourced data library (query, loader, action) already covers it.
- Do not call backend shapes you have not read. Align form fields and API payloads with actual types/schemas.

## What not to do

- No lorem ipsum, “Welcome to your app,” or placeholder company names when real copy exists or was given.
- No new animation library, icon pack, or component library unless the user asked and the repo does not already provide one.
- No comments that restate the JSX. No drive-by refactors of unrelated components.
